  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Core demand remains soft, but product innovation is gaining traction. Early adoption of the newer bunion systems is expanding, with existing Lapiplasty surgeons adding the new options and fresh surgeons entering the fold. Upcoming launches like SuperBite, SpeedXM, and Lapiplasty Lightning could broaden the procedural base. Favorable FDA designations and promising clinical results recently lifted sentiment, while an ownership change has added strategic intrigue. Still, the revenue trajectory is guided to stay subdued, suggesting competitive and end-market headwinds persist.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is pairing cost discipline with a product-led revival. They trimmed operating expenses and are targeting a meaningful reduction in cash consumption this year. Full-year guidance was reaffirmed, signaling confidence that new system rollouts will gradually stabilize the business. The quarterly beat and early surgeon uptake offer some validation, but sustained losses temper confidence in the recovery’s speed. Investor attention now rests on whether the innovation pipeline can rekindle growth.",
